    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office first opened in the community of Bancroft on May 17, 1876.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bancroft%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The geography of Bancroft is mostly flat, though two prominent bluffs rise above the level plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bancroft%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mosquito Bluff is a large east-west ridge in Bancroft that is now split into two hills by Harding Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bancroft%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Ledge is a prominent bluff in Bancroft that has been known as Lover's Leap, Hellfire Hill, and High Rock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bancroft%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "An ichnite rock at the top of The Ledge in Bancroft has preserved traces of the passage of Climactichnites.",
